WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.000
I want to fund a Bitcoin prize today,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.010
but I don’t know who’ll win,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.050
or which wallet they’ll use.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.630
With PrizeKey,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.010
I fund a gift first,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.950
pass its NEAR claim to the winner,

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.450
and let them choose where Bitcoin goes.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.500
Let me show you.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.450
In this earlier test,

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.530
I funded a gift with 20,000 test sats.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.750
It has its own Bitcoin address.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.350
Once I have a winner,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.680
I enter their NEAR account

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.120
and pass them the claim.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.150
I don’t need their Bitcoin address.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.750
Now they’re the holder.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.970
They choose where to receive the Bitcoin,

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.750
and approve the payout.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.400
NEAR Chain Signatures authorizes it,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.450
then the browser sends Bitcoin.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.550
This earlier test used a terminal wallet.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.050
Here’s what the recipient sees today.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.550
19,750 test sats delivered,

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.150
after a 250-sat fee.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.350
If they want to check,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.500
the transaction is right here.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.900
Fund the prize first.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.150
Let the winner choose where it goes.
